    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0288" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14911/92.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Refering to the department’s telegram of
                    the 20th ultimo,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d215-f1"/> I transmit herewith your
                    commission as ambassador extraordinary to represent this Government at the
                    ceremonies which are to take place in May next incident upon the burial of the
                    remains of His Majesty Kwang-hsü, late Emperor of China.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. C. O’Loughlin.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
